# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# customizations/document-quick-change.toml — Layer 5 (team)
#
# COMMITTED. Team-edited. Example for the `document-quick-change` skill (the
# first quick-dev skill — captures the combined lightweight spec).
#
# This example expresses a team that pulls the change's requirements straight
# from a JIRA story instead of hand-capturing them, using an installed
# Atlassian add-on.
#
# A sibling `document-quick-change.user.toml` (gitignored) can do the same at
# higher precedence for your personal overrides.
#
# See config/SCHEMAS.md § 2.6 (tool resolution) and
# references/orientation/source-adapters.md (the source-adapter convention).
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────


# ─── Source adapter (OPTIONAL) ───────────────────────────────────────────────
# Names an installed add-on skill that seeds the quick-dev spec's existing-
# artifact intake (Step 3) from an external system. Here: pull a JIRA story
# into a structured package on disk and seed the spec from it.
#
# Requires the Atlassian add-on repo to be installed and discoverable, plus a
# matching [tools.atlassian] block in project.toml. If the adapter is set but
# not installed, the skill surfaces the gap and falls back to asking you
# directly. Unset (the default) = capture by direct elicitation.

requirements_source = "jira-extract-requirements"
